# Pinned inputs are held to their owners' SHA-256, and the Windows vein reads
# them from its own checkout: no platform may rewrite a committed byte, line
# endings included.
* -text
# The one exception is read by cmd.exe, which parses a batch file by CRLF
# lines: on 21.10, once gate.cmd came out with LF, every verb behind it hung
# on windows-latest while the binary called directly answered.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
